## Protected legacy compatibility identities

| Identity | Protected surface | Required invariant |
|---|---|---|
| Pinned baseline | `docs/baseline/musubix3-v0.1.18-cli-help.json` | Remains a faithful musubix3 v0.1.18 compatibility fixture and retains its `musubix3` commands and help text. |
| Legacy source repository | `isRecognizedMusubixSource(manifest)` in `packages/analysis/src/files.ts` | Continues to recognize only the exact legacy pair `name: "musubix3"` and repository URL `https://github.com/nahisaho/musubix3.git`, alongside the current exact musubix5 pair. |
| Solver environment | Formal CLI/runtime and `legacySolverCommands(environment)` | Retains the public names `MUSUBIX3_Z3` and `MUSUBIX3_LEAN`; no `MUSUBIX5_*` replacement or alias is introduced by this feature. |
| Attestation key binding | `githubOidcAudience(...)` in `packages/analysis/src/attestation.ts` | Retains the fragments `musubix3-key-id` and `musubix3-key-sha256` so existing verifier bindings remain stable. |
| Compatibility oracle package | `BASELINE_IDENTITY.package` in `packages/analysis/src/compatibility-oracle.ts` | Remains exactly `musubix3`, identifying the pinned oracle rather than the current package. |

## DES-M5-WAVE1-NAMING-001: Current-name output boundary
Responsibilities: Replace the retired product token at exactly the five #11-owned recovery-guidance and generated-artifact surfaces numbered 2 through 6, consume the #25-owned surface 1 as an integration dependency, and leave every protected legacy compatibility identity unchanged.
Interfaces: Write-owned interfaces `validateModelCorrespondenceEvidence(root)` in `packages/analysis/src/model-correspondence.ts`, the initial quality-reason and `.gitignore` comment outputs of `install(root, packageRoot, options)` in `packages/cli/src/install.ts`, and `generateSmt2(model)` plus `generateLean(model)` in `packages/analysis/src/formal.ts`; dependency-provided read-only integration contract `loadTrace(root)` from `DES-M5-WAVE1-TRACE-002`.
Constraints: GitHub issue #11 must not edit `packages/analysis/src/trace.ts`; GitHub issue #25 and `DES-M5-WAVE1-TRACE-002` exclusively own the surface 1 token replacement and must supply `Trace graph missing; run musubix5 trace build.` exactly. This component changes only surfaces 2 through 6 and must produce their required strings exactly. ADR-0028 and `DES-M5-WAVE1-TRACE-003` own install trace persistence, shared-index actions, and legacy removal; this naming feature changes only the enumerated quality reason and `.gitignore` comment strings within the resulting install control flow. The SMT header changes only its `musubix3` token and retains the complete trailing sentence `This checks only the documented explicit constraint model.`. The Lean header retains the complete first line `/- Generated by musubix5.` after the same token-only replacement. No diagnostic code, shared-index schema, trace path, newline convention, formal expression, or install merge semantics outside those two named strings changes. `musubix3` remains valid only on the protected surfaces listed above; historical and baseline artifacts are not regenerated. No executable alias, environment-variable alias, repository-identity normalization, or attestation migration is added.
Requirements: REQ-M5-WAVE1-NAMING-001
ADRs: ADR-0002 ADR-0018 ADR-0028
Depends-On: DES-M5-WAVE1-TRACE-002

## DES-M5-WAVE1-NAMING-002: Product-name regression contract
Responsibilities: Provide one authoritative regression test whose #11 Red fails on at least one of the five #11-owned surfaces without depending on the trace diagnostic, and whose post-#25 Green proves all six current-name outputs while guarding every protected legacy compatibility identity against accidental broad replacement.
Interfaces: `TEST-M5-WAVE1-PRODUCT-NAMING-001` in `tests/product-name-guidance.test.ts`; #11-owned public outputs from `validateModelCorrespondenceEvidence`, `generateSmt2`, `generateLean`, and CLI `install`; post-dependency read-only `loadTrace` output supplied by `DES-M5-WAVE1-TRACE-002`; public analysis exports `isRecognizedMusubixSource`, `legacySolverCommands`, `githubOidcAudience`, and `BASELINE_IDENTITY`; pinned baseline fixture `docs/baseline/musubix3-v0.1.18-cli-help.json`.
Constraints: Red is established before #11 implementation by an assertion against at least one of surfaces 2 through 6 and must not require, modify, or use failure of surface 1. After `DES-M5-WAVE1-TRACE-002` is integrated, Green exercises observable output rather than only searching production source and asserts all six exact required strings: the dependency-owned missing trace diagnostic, missing model-correspondence diagnostic, initial quality reason, generated `.gitignore` comment, full SMT header `; Generated by musubix5. This checks only the documented explicit constraint model.`, and full Lean first line `/- Generated by musubix5.`. The test must reject the retired product token on those six outputs. The SMT assertion must prove the trailing sentence is retained and only the naming token changed; the Lean assertion must compare the complete first line. In the same test node, it must assert that the pinned baseline still contains its legacy command identity, the exact musubix3 repository pair remains recognized, `MUSUBIX3_Z3` and `MUSUBIX3_LEAN` remain accepted names, both `musubix3-key-*` attestation fragments remain stable, and `BASELINE_IDENTITY.package` remains `musubix3`. Temporary consumer workspaces are isolated and cleaned up; no repository evidence or trace artifact is generated by the test.
Requirements: REQ-M5-WAVE1-NAMING-001
ADRs: ADR-0002 ADR-0018 ADR-0028
Depends-On: DES-M5-WAVE1-NAMING-001 DES-M5-WAVE1-TRACE-002
